    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25xjkSizeFBrzHTULVxNtCU)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on current `main` (after #526, #527); independent of the other open PRs.\n- Touches `sp-cite-match.el` (via `docs/tangles/academic/sp-cite-match.org`) and two test files.\n\n## What I found\n\n- `C-c o s` (`sp-sourcerefs-convert`) failed with `Invalid search bound (wrong side of point)`.\n- Not the region or point handling in `sp-sourcerefs`: I ran it with and without a region, on the last line without a newline, with a reference list and with an existing Cited works block, all fine.\n- The cause is in the BibTeX reader of `sp-cite-match`, which every command here calls first (`sp-cite-match-candidates`):\n  - an entry was assumed to end at the next line that starts with `@`;\n  - a field value can contain such a line (e.g. an abstract with `\\n@handle`);\n  - the value reader then moved point past that bound, and the next `re-search-forward` with the old bound signalled the error.\n- Reproduced with a two-entry `.bib` whose abstract has a line `@lab for details`; the same bug would have hit `Ctrl+Shift+K` and `sp-cite-open` on such a library.\n\n## What changed\n\n- New `sp-cite-match--entry-end`: a brace entry ends at its matching closing brace. Fallback (parenthesis entries, unbalanced braces) is the old rule, the next `@` line.\n- The field loop also stops when point is at or past the end, so it cannot search with a bound behind point.\n- Docs: bullets in \"Reading the BibTeX records\" in `sp-cite-match.org`; `.el` re-tangled. `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `sp-cite-match-test.el`: abstract with an `@` line (both entries read, fields after the abstract kept), last entry without a trailing newline, unbalanced braces, parenthesis entry, entry end never before its start.\n- `sp-sourcerefs-test.el`: convert with no region, last line without a newline, point at the end of the buffer, region boundaries (second line only, cut inside a line, whole buffer through the region path), no lines is a user error.\n\n## Checked by Claude\n\n- Emacs 29.3 batch: `sp-cite-match-test.el` 22 of 22 pass (17 old + 5 new); `sp-sourcerefs-test.el` 10 of 10 pass; `check-parens` OK; `tools/check-tangle.sh`: all modules match their docs.\n- The reproduction fails before the change (`Invalid search bound`) and gives 2 entries after.\n- Not run: `tests/sp-cite-open-test.el` (needs the DEVONthink modules, not loadable here), your real `.bib` files, `C-c o s` in a GUI Emacs. I have not seen your actual `.bib`, so I assume an `@` line inside a field is what triggered it for you; if the error stays, send me the entry it stops at.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/academic -l ert -l tests/sp-cite-match-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` passes\n- [x] `emacs -Q --batch -l ert -l tests/sp-sourcerefs-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` passes\n- [ ] Restart Emacs (or reload `sp-cite-match`), then `C-c o s` in a litnote with `- SOURCEREFS Smith 2017`: no error, a report buffer opens\n- [ ] Confirm the line becomes `[cite:@key]` and the `Cited works` table appears\n- [ ] Regression: `Ctrl+Shift+K` in DEVONthink still writes the Cited works section\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9taQEBJAWpQmkyfLY)_",
